- Good luck, bro.

01:41:12.928 --> 01:41:14.170
- [Louis] All right, man keep--

01:41:14.170 --> 01:41:15.170
- Yo, sorry.

01:41:16.903 --> 01:41:20.484
This burnout thing like what, like who?

01:41:20.484 --> 01:41:22.230
Once you eliminate the judgment

01:41:22.230 --> 01:41:24.730
of people around your failure.

01:41:26.119 --> 01:41:28.059
I love when people try to
say shit about my failure.

01:41:28.059 --> 01:41:30.756
I'm like, what about you?

01:41:30.756 --> 01:41:31.706
You know, right?

01:41:31.706 --> 01:41:35.362
Like seriously though, especially parents.

01:41:35.362 --> 01:41:36.821
Especially siblings.

01:41:36.821 --> 01:41:40.178
Nobody's remotely close to perfect.

01:41:40.178 --> 01:41:42.961
- [Man] Do you think burnout's
related to impatience?

01:41:42.961 --> 01:41:44.186
- It could be.

01:41:44.186 --> 01:41:46.014
I think it's a really thoughtful question.

01:41:46.014 --> 01:41:48.587
I do think burnout sometimes

01:41:48.587 --> 01:41:51.406
is what people manifest impatience into,

01:41:51.406 --> 01:41:52.653
and they think they're burnt out,

01:41:52.653 --> 01:41:54.563
but what is was really was entitlement.

01:41:54.563 --> 01:41:56.883
And it's actually them like
(imitating baby crying)

01:41:56.883 --> 01:41:58.502
kicking, and screaming, you know?

01:41:58.502 --> 01:42:01.180
But other times it's mental burnout.

01:42:01.180 --> 01:42:02.272
There's a lot of people that burn.

01:42:02.272 --> 01:42:06.678
And burnout, again, look I
think we have to be very careful

01:42:06.678 --> 01:42:07.511
when we talk about these things.

01:42:07.511 --> 01:42:08.809
There's people that have
mental health issues

01:42:08.809 --> 01:42:11.061
versus people that put over-stress

01:42:11.061 --> 01:42:13.420
on themselves versus mom situation.

01:42:13.420 --> 01:42:16.845
He's got a mom situation,
and now he's on a plane.

01:42:16.845 --> 01:42:18.646
So, when I talk about these things

01:42:18.646 --> 01:42:19.899
I don't have all the context.

01:42:19.899 --> 01:42:22.647
I don't want anybody to ever think...

01:42:22.647 --> 01:42:26.695
That Paulo kid was taking
some of my stuff very blindly.

01:42:26.695 --> 01:42:27.813
I'm worried about that stuff,

01:42:27.813 --> 01:42:31.331
but yeah, man that dude is not burnt out.

01:42:31.331 --> 01:42:33.820
That dude is just worried
about the ramifications

01:42:33.820 --> 01:42:36.070
if he doesn't like his job.

01:42:37.971 --> 01:42:38.804
Quit.

01:42:38.804 --> 01:42:41.498
Nobody's looking at your fucking resume.

01:42:41.498 --> 01:42:42.616
They don't give a fuck if you've

01:42:42.616 --> 01:42:44.317
worked somewhere for three months.

01:42:44.317 --> 01:42:46.400
Blame it on a crazy boss.

01:42:48.259 --> 01:42:49.795
People do anyway.

01:42:49.795 --> 01:42:50.714
I fired a fuck load of people

01:42:50.714 --> 01:42:53.631
that suck shit then blame it on me.

01:42:56.638 --> 01:42:59.305
(line trilling)

01:43:10.041 --> 01:43:11.636
It's a fun night.

01:43:11.636 --> 01:43:14.425
I like the random calling.

01:43:14.425 --> 01:43:17.426
I feel better about--
(ringing drowns out Gary)

01:43:17.426 --> 01:43:18.919
I like it also with like the last couple

01:43:18.919 --> 01:43:21.079
of times I had to sell empathy, you know?

01:43:21.079 --> 01:43:22.989
Just like--
(ringing drowns out Gary)

01:43:22.989 --> 01:43:26.846
Fucking buying people million
dollar insurance and shit.

